    <statement><p>The position of a particle moving along the <m>x</m>-axis is given
by <m>s(t) = 5t^{2}+5</m>.  Use difference quotients to find the
velocity <m>v(t)</m> and acceleration <m>a(t)</m>, filling in the following
expressions as you do so:</p>
<p><m>v(t) = \lim\limits_{h\to0}</m>
[ <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0001"/> / h ] = <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p><m>a(t) = \lim\limits_{h\to0}</m>
[ <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0003"/> / h ] = <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0004"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>5\mathopen{}\left(t+h\right)^{2}+5-\left(5t^{2}+5\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>10t</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>10\mathopen{}\left(t+h\right)-10t</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>10</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><me>v(t) = \lim_{h\to0} \frac{5\mathopen{}\left(t+h\right)^{2}+5 - 5t^{2}+5}{h}
        = \lim_{h\to0} \frac{5t^{2}+10th+5h^{2}+5-5t^{2}-5}{h}
        = \lim_{h\to0} 10t+5h = 10 t</me>
and
<me>v(t) = \lim_{h\to0} \frac{10\mathopen{}\left(t+h\right) - 10t}{h}
        = \lim_{h\to0} \frac{10t+10h-10t}{h}
        = \lim_{h\to0} 10 = 10.</me>



</solution>
